      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Esianti: Palace of the Winds [zone=1211]\n**Who:**\n- Joyous Blossom [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Crisp stack of papers [item=135802]\n- Singed stack of papers [item=135803]\n- Stack of insults [item=135806]\n- Stained, singed stack of papers [item=135804]\n- Stained, singed, stabbed stack of papers [item=135805]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Hammer Tearing Strike [npc=54252]\n- Lydia Springstrong [npc=54364]\n- Sadness of Distant Mountains [npc=54367]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Brass Palace [quest=9445]\n- Fight Fire [quest=9263]\n- Key to the Kingdom [quest=9264]\n- Palace of Embers [quest=9433]\n- Prisoner's Dilemma [quest=9265]\n- Soldier of Air [quest=9225]\n- Trial of Three (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9281]\n- Trial of the Ashes of Rusted Cliff's Glory (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9335]\n- Trial of the Eternal Cyclone (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9336]\n- Trial of the Speaker's Amphitheater (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9282]\n- Trial of the Wending Ways (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9337]\n**Era:** | !The Burning Lands\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 4 04:26:41 2018\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | Prerequisite Quests: Soldier of Air, Fight Fire, any one Trial of Smoke, Prisoner's Dilemma, Palace of Embers, Brass Palace, and Key to the Kingdom.\nFind Joyous Blossom in Esianti at -213, -1591, -62 on the far east island across the bridge near the west edge, she is on the Find tool.\nYou say, 'Hail, Joyous Blossom'\nJoyous Blossom says, 'Hey, have you seen Sadness of Distant Mountains? Bring [this] to him.'\nYou say, ' What's this?'\nShe gives you Crisp stack of papers.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Of Mice and Jann'.\n\n---\n\n2. Deliver the Crisp stack of papers to Sadness of Distant Mountains 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** Joyous Blossom asked you to hand deliver what appears to be some documents to Sadness of Distant Mountains because apparently you have that kind of time on hand and they don't, being immortal and all.\n\n\n\n\nYou would think that the jann would have been able to perform their own menial tasks by now.\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Crisp stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nSadness of Distant Mountains is fuming as he is going over piles of paperwork\n\n\n\n\nHe gives you Crisp stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nSadness of Distant Mountains begins to read through some of the information in the packet, his expression sours as he gets to the end of the summons, 'Well I never!'. He furiously begins to write in the packet of paper\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nHe is still writing.\n\n\n\n\nHe gets more livid with each of his quill strokes.\n\n\n\n\nIt feels like he may never stop writing.\n\n\n\n\nSadness of Distant Mountains says, 'Give Hammer Tearing Strike my rebuttal, I will NOT have him casting these disparaging remarks upon the Djinn!''\n\n3. Deliver Sadness of Distant Mountain's rebuttal to Hammer Tearing Strike 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** Well, THAT was unexpected.\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Crisp stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike greets you with a smile 'Why hello mortal, how can I assist yo...' he stops talking abruptly and notices the packet of papers you handed him. He becomes furious as he slams the packet on a desk, pulls out a quill and begins to write in the packets, murmuring curses under his breath.\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Singed stack of papers [quest=9447]\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says, '\"I cannot believe he would...HMPH\"'\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike breaks a quill, throws it across the desk and furiously grabs another one. He dips it in a nearby inkwell and continues writing...\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike gets near the end of the parchment and says '... YOURS... TRUELY... Deliver this to Lydia Springstrong immediately!' in his rage he singed part of the parchment.\n\n4. Deliver Hammer Tearing Strike's retort to Lydia Springstrong 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** At least you learned a few new Efreeti curse words. Hopefully Lydia will be able to cool the tempers of these two.\n\n\n\n\nUpon handing Lydia Springstrong Singed stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nLydia Springstrong says, 'Greetings adventurer! What can I help you with?' as you hand Lydia the packet of papers, her expression goes from jovial to dire. 'Oh no...' she grabs a quill and an inkpot nervously. 'No no no...''\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nLydia Springstrong's hand is shaking as she is scratching words into the paper, saying while she continues with her missive, 'Please...refrain...from...further...'\n\n\n\n\nLydia Springstrong continues writing, saying aloud '...and it would be in best interest to the mortal races if we could come to a consensus...'\n\n\n\n\nLydia Springstrong spills some of her ink during her nervous scrawling, 'Earnestly yours...'\n\n\n\n\nLydia Springstrong says, 'Please bring this back to Hammer Tearing Strike, I hope we are not too late.'\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Stained, singed stack of papers [quest=9447]\n\n5. Deliver Lydia Springstrong's counterargument to Hammer Tearing Strike 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** This packet has seen some better days\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Hammer Tearing Strike'\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike is waiting for you to do what you were told.\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Stained, singed stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike grabs the singed and stained stack of papers from your hand before you have a chance to say anything and begins to read.\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says, 'Mmhmm.'\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says 'Very well.' as he sets the papers down and begins writing again.\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says, 'Tell me mortal, how is it that you [started: It all started when...] being a delivery person? Why is this the way you wanted to spend your life?'\n\n\n\n\nBefore you could even answer, Hammer Tearing Strike interrupts you, 'That's fascinating, please bring my protest to Sadness of Distant Mountains'\n\n\n\n\nYou receive Stained, singed stack of papers [quest=9447].\n\n\n\n\nYou say, ' It all started when...'\n\n6. Deliver Hammer Tearing Strike's protest to Sadness of Distant Mountains 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** While rude, you hope that this will help smooth things over between the Djinn and the Efreeti.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Sadness of Distant Mountains'\n\n\n\n\nSadness of Distant Mountains is waiting for you to do what you were told\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Stained, singed stack of papers [quest=9447]\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nSadness of Distant Mountains seems to visually try to maintain his composure in seeing you, and takes the singed and stained stack of papers from you calmly, as if trying to hold back his rage. 'Thank you mortal, I didn't mean to explode at you like I did, I don't think this is your fault, and it wasn't fair that I would respond to you the way I did.' He continues to read through the papers, and begins to start a response. This time his curses are met with clenched jaws, as if a tide of anger is swelling up inside of him, and finishes his writing with a flourish and a stab of the quill. 'Please give this to Hammer Tearing Strike.'\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Stained, singed, stabbed stack of papers [quest=9447]\n\n7. Deliver Sadness of Distant Mountain's grievance to Hammer Tearing Strike 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** It appears that whatever Lydia wrote helped diffuse the situation between the two\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Stained, singed, stabbed stack of papers to Hammer Tearing Strike.\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says, 'You again, good, I wanted to see what Sadness of Distant Mountains' response was going to be.' Hammer Tearing Strike begins to read the singed, stabbed, torn, stained pack of papers. He smiles, and begins to write again.'\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nHammer Tearing Strike says, 'Thank you for your help in this matter mortal, it was very nice knowing you. Please bring this back to Sadness of Distant Mountains.'\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Stained, singed, stabbed stack of papers [quest=9447]\n\n8. Deliver Hammer Tearing Strike's challenge to Sadness of the Distant Mountains 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** That was pretty foreboding. You have an ill feeling in the pit of your stomach, as if you were an accessory to a conflict opening up someplace else in the Planes of Power.\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Stained, singed, stabbed stack of papers [quest=9447] to Sadness of the Distant Mountains.\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\n'If it is a fight he wants, then it's a fight he will get! Begone mortal, I have work to do.' Sadness of Distant Mountains throws the stack of papers back at you.\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Stack of insults [quest=9447]\n\n9. Bring the Stack of insults to Joyous Blossom 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n\n\n\n**Task Window:** Perhaps Joyous Blossom will be able to shed some light as to what had happened today.\n\n\n\n\nUpon hand in of Stack of insults [quest=9447] to Joyous Blossom.\n\n\n\n\nJoyous Blossom takes the packet and begins to read it.\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Of Mice and Jann' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nYou leave Joyous Blossom even more confused than when you first met her.\n\n\n\n\nYou receive 5 gold .\n\n\nYou receive 212 platinum .\n\n\nYou gain experience!\n\n\n\n\nJoyous Blossom bellows out the loudest laugh you have ever heard from an ondine, and then pretends you no longer exist.\n\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n212 platinum 5 gold\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
