 No, no, you are here because you want something. I do remember asking you to do a task for me to learn about entry to [Mearatas]. Did you [forget] the name I gave you earlier?'\nYou say, 'forget'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Earthen Dirge'.\nObsidian Sundering Master sighs, 'Of course. You should seek Dirge in the Catacomb. He has a way in, all you need to do is convince him to let you use it.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Convince Dirge in the Catacomb to let you use his portal. 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n> **Task Window:** You have been given a name of someone that might have access to Mearatas, Dirge in the Catacombs. You need to find him and convince him to give you access to the duende castle.\n>\n> You will probably have to carefully, manipulate Dirge in the Catacombs. Obsidian Sundering Master suggested that you use your relative fame among the djinn and the fact that you know Dirge in the Catacombs has set up a portal that he certainly should not have to your best advantage. Maybe threaten to tell other that you know about his secret entrance to Mearatas.\nYou say, 'Hail, Dirge in the Catacomb'\nDirge in the Catacomb looks over his nose down upon you. After a pause and with a sneer in his voice, 'A mortal, of course. We are infested with them. What must I do to get you to leave Esianti and never return? Not that I would trust you to leave no matter what I were to give you.'\nYou say, 'I heard something about a portal?'\nDirge in the Catacomb says, 'Should I find a way to get you into Mearatas and you were to be discovered, your presence would be a danger to me. However, should you find yourself in that place and discover the head of a duende called Funereal Dust Warrior and return it to my agent in the city, well then I might no longer be concerned. Someone that, even through no fault of their own, were to kill a duende in the city would have more to fear than anything they could cause to happen to me.'\nSay \"something\"\nYour task 'Earthen Dirge' has been updated.\nDirge in the Catacomb says, 'Should I find a way to get you into Mearatas and you were to be discovered, your presence would be a danger to me. However, should you find yourself in that place and discover the head of a duende called Funereal Dust Warrior and return it to my agent in the city, well then I might no longer be concerned. Someone that, even through no fault of their own, were to kill a duende in the city would have more to fear than anything they could cause to happen to me.'\n2\\. Defeat Funereal Dust Warrior and recover his head. 0/1 Mearatas: The Stone Demesne\n> **Task Window:** Your task seems simple but the djinn implied that he was asking you to do something that would put you at risk and give him leverage over you should you choose to reveal his secret.\nFunereal Dust Warrior is located in the north eastern section of Mearatas on the outside ring. Attack him.\nFunereal Dust Warrior says, 'You do not have a warrant to be here. I must end your poor mortal existence.'\nLoot Head of Funereal Dust Warrior from its corpse.\n3\\. Deliver 1 Head of Funereal Dust Warrior to Dirge in the Catacombs. 0/1 Esianti: Palace of the Winds\n> **Task Window:** Simply bring the head to Dirge in the Catacomb's assistant.\nGive Head of Funereal Dust Warrior to Dirge in the Catacombs.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum 6 gold 6 silver 7 copper\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Gidono\n- 141pp, 6g, 6s, 7cp, Experience",
