re running this mission again, say \"key\" to Obsidian Sundering Master.\nOtherwise:\nYou say, 'Hail, Obsidian Sundering Master'\nObsidian Sundering Master says, 'You do seem to like the view here. Or perhaps it's my company? No, no, you are here because you want something. I do remember asking you to do a task for me to learn about entry to [Mearatas]. Did you [forget] the name I gave you earlier?'\nYou say, 'mold seeker'\nObsidian Sundering Master says, 'I have heard rumors of what the rebel efreeti hopes to do. So you are the agent of that change. That confirmation of the rumor has value to me, as well as connecting your face with all this. For that, I will give you a hint. Someone in Mearatas will know where that duende mold is kept. The worst that can happen is that you ask someone and they are offended and try to kill you. That should be something you are well used to dealing with. In a way I wish you luck. Should you succeed your name and face may become extremely valuable to me.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Mold Seeker'.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Find out where the duende keep their unused female mold. 0/1 Mearatas: The Stone Demease\n> **Task Window :** Somewhere in this city you hope to find a mold in the shape of a female duende that you are expected to find and steal for Fennin Ro.\n>\n> See if anyone here will tell you where the duende mold is. There seems to be a good chance that this will upset some of the locals.\nHead to the North Eastern section and ask \"Where is the female duende mold?\" to mobs. Some will ignore you, others will attack.\nA granite envoy says, 'Our relics are not for you to discuss. You do not even belong here!\nEventually one will tell you where the duende mold is.\nA vekerchiki warrior says, 'If you have questions about our relics, speak with the relic keeper, not me.'\nYour task 'Mold Seeker' has been updated.\n2\\. Speak with the relic keeper and see if you can find out where the mold is kept. 0/1 Mearatas: The Stone Demease\n> **Task Window :** Find this relic keeper and see if it will show you the relics.\nBattleworn Obelisk [npc=54622] spawns at /loc 525,-290.\nYou say, 'Hail, Battleworn Obelisk'\nBattleworn Obelisk says, 'Hello, stranger. Odd, seeing you here. There are been so few mortals in Mearatas for such a very long time. If there are questions you have, I may be able to answer them. I am something of an historian, it is my task to watch over artifacts of our past and to know why they are important.'\nYou say, 'Would you show me the relics?'\nBattleworn Obelisk says, 'Hmm, I don't think I can give you access to our relics. It is my duty to guard the key and I am only to give access to the relics when appropriate. A few religious items must be present at some rituals. Some contracts need to be reviewed at times. Sometimes a historic criminal needs to be spoken with. All of these things happen with the delivery of an appropriate contract. I know you have no such contract, for no mortal ever will. I am afraid that I can not allow you into the relic chamber.'\nYour task 'Mold Seeker' has been updated.\n3\\. Get the relic keeper's key. 0/1 Mearatas: The Stone Demease\n> **Task Window :** You seem to have no other option.\nKill Battleworn Obelisk.\nBattleworn Obelisk says, 'So, you have done as asked. I admit surprise. As you are a mere mortal, must remind you that what you have done puts you in danger, should anyone find a need to report your actions to an Udex of the duende. So long as you keep that in mind, You shall have access to this portal, as promised.'\nBattleworn Obelisk's corpse avalanches to the ground.\nBattleworn Obelisk has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\n4\\. Pick up the relic keeper's key. 0/1 Mearatas: The Stone Demease\nLoot the Key of the Relic Keeper [item=134609] to complete the task. It will be later used to trigger Relic Raider [quest=9462].\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum 6 gold 6 silver 7 copper\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Larth, Veludeus\n- Platinum, Experience",
